      "[2026-08-03-italian-ui-layer-and-guided-tour] No dependency change; `package.json` gains one entry in the `verify:l10n` chain.",
      "[2026-08-03-l10n-explain-channel] **`explain` had no side-table channel, and two releases shipped without their own definition of done.** The per-source trio is #72 (UI strings), #71 (fono respellings) and **#60 (explanations in the native language)**. The side tables carried `prompt / promptNative / options / wrongNote / distractorNotes` — never `explain`, which `flattenBank` read straight off the base bank. So the only way to give a source language its own explanations was to edit the giant banks in place, which is what v3.0 and v3.1 did for en and es. v3.2 (pt) and v3.3 (fr) did not, and nothing caught it.",
      "[2026-08-03-l10n-explain-channel] · Measured through the real path (`flattenBank` + the play screen's own `resolveExplainText`):",
